Lojban is not -- and never was intended to be -- a philosophical language, =
in which everything received a appropriate name derived from a few "semanti=
c primes".  If gismu overlap, this is typically because natural languages h=
ave found it Convenient to have more than one word in that area.  Lojban ha=
s generally followed these natural patterns (with notable exceptions, like =
'klama').  Probably more overall simplicity could be achieved by adding gis=
mu even with overlaps (most words in English can be replaced by other words=
 or short phrases in the intricate  cycles of definitions).

